# UI Design Skill v0.6.0

When working on a UI page:

1. Read `ui-design/manifest.yaml` when it exists. Identify the skill version, asset schema version, project profile, and default theme.
2. Prefer to keep and read the existing Design Tokens, Component Registry, and target Page Schema. A skill upgrade does not rewrite assets or code.
3. Inspect the component library and icon library actually installed in the frontend project. Map project wrappers first, then library components and tokens.
4. Reuse components inside the theme boundary registered for admin, visualization, or hybrid projects. Do not apply styles from one profile globally to another.
5. For a new page, analyze the structure and create or incrementally update the Page Schema before writing code.
6. Follow the shared project component theme by default. Create a constrained variant only when the user explicitly asks for reference fidelity or a theme change.
7. For icons that will be reused, look for source assets or the project icon library first. Read the icon asset rules when the task needs them.
8. After implementation, preview and verify structure, components, theme, overlays, states, icons, and responsive layout.

Read the relevant files in `.cursor/skills/ui-design/references/` when a decision needs the detailed rules.
